  "headline": "Bailey leads by one as a Bench Boost blitz detonates BFL Gameweek 1.",
  "summary": "David Bailey’s Dave's Dream Team took Manager of the Week honours with 67 points and the early BFL lead, just one point clear of Will Finney and olly barnes. With the top four separated by only 3 points after a frantic Bench Boost opening, the title race is already absurdly tight.",
  "report": "David Bailey has drawn first blood in Biddenham Fantasy League season 2627, banking 67 points with Dave's Dream Team to take top spot. It is a one-point lead, though: Will Finney’s 0v3rf1tt3d.h5 sits on 66, with olly barnes and Grasshoppers another point back on 65. Jamie Mitchell’s wataru doing? is fourth on 64, meaning the top four are covered by just 3 points. No easing into this one.\n\nBailey was Manager of the Week with a clean 67-point net score, 18.9 points above the league average of 48.1 and well ahead of the 50-point global average. His rise of 9 places put him straight into first, while amy warden surged 10 places into fifth with Palmer Violets on 63. Paul Alexis was the week’s biggest climber, up 12 places after scoring 51.\n\nThe Bench Boost button was very much in fashion. Bailey, Finney, olly barnes and Jamie Mitchell all played bboost, and they occupy the top four places. That leaves 19 bench boosts remaining in the league, while all 25 managers still have their triple captain and free hit intact.\n\nBailey’s route to the summit included a 13-point Stach differential for LEE, owned by him alone, plus 11-point White, shared only with olly barnes. Grasshoppers had their own sharp pick in Ødegaard’s 11 points, while amy warden joined Dan Birkinshaw in benefiting from Palmer’s 13 points. Elsewhere, Phil Johnson had the league’s biggest differential return through M.Sangaré of BRE on 14, and Mark Horton found 13 points from BRE’s Kayode despite ending the week on 43 and falling 10 places.\n\nCaptaincy was less glamorous. Haaland was the popular choice, selected by 18 managers, but returned only 2 points. Will Finney’s Haaland armband is the official howler despite his excellent 66-point total; a reminder that even the captaincy sting could not derail that Bench Boost. Abi Speight supplied the captaincy genius, doubling Havertz’s 6 points.\n\nThere was pain further down too. James Marshall left 20 points on the bench, while Callum Bowness’s Schär Me the Money collected the wooden spoon on 30. Chris Beeden is also the coldest manager on the early form table with 30 from the last 3, while Vaughan Cosbie-Ross fell 11 places after scoring 39. James Geary dropped 10 places despite a 50-point week.\n\nFor now, Bailey holds the crown, but it is a precarious one: one point to Finney, one more to olly barnes, then one more to Mitchell. The BFL title race has started with four managers practically sharing the same seat.",
